  "findings": [
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "runtime-dirs-not-shipped",
      "lines": [
        "3rdparty/ is read at run time and is not in the shipped file set: lib/Service/ExtractorGetID3.php:41 reaches it through __DIR__.",
        "fonts/ is read at run time and is not in the shipped file set: lib/Utility/PlaceholderImage.php:97 reaches it through __DIR__.",
        "  A release ships only the paths of the keep set (the ncmake core and ncmake.mk), so the tarball lacks them and the app fails in the code that reads them, while the build and the packing pass. In ncmake.mk, keep_extra += 3rdparty fonts ships them."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "nextcloud-support",
      "lines": [
        "Declares Nextcloud 20 to 32; the oldest maintained major is 32 (as of 2026-09), the newest released 35 (the release tags of nextcloud/server).",
        "  min-version 20 reaches below the oldest maintained major (32), which means the code has to keep working with APIs that are no longer tested upstream."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "php-support",
      "lines": [
        "PHP floor stated once: appinfo/info.xml min-version 7.4; composer.json states no php requirement.",
        "  Nothing contradicts anything here. Stating it in both places is what keeps a composer install from resolving packages for a PHP the server will not run."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "php-support-max",
      "lines": [
        "appinfo/info.xml caps PHP at max-version 8.4.",
        "  A server on a newer PHP refuses to enable the app, so this cap has to be raised deliberately with every PHP release, not left where it was."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "node-version",
      "lines": [
        "No Node version is stated: no engines.node, no .nvmrc, and no node-version in the installed workflows.",
        "  Whoever builds the app uses whatever Node they have, and a build that works on one machine is then not evidence for the next."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "tooling",
      "lines": [
        "Tooling in the checkout: PHPUnit (tests/php/unit/phpunit.xml), PHP-CS-Fixer (.php-cs-fixer.dist.php).",
        " No ESLint configuration: nothing checks the frontend sources, so a wrong import is found by the build or not at all.",
        " No Stylelint configuration: stylesheets are unchecked, and a mistake in CSS fails silently instead of loudly.",
        " No Psalm configuration: the PHP side has no static analysis, which is what catches a wrong type before the server does.",
        " No REUSE configuration: licensing is not machine-checkable, which the App Store and every distribution ask for.",
        " No EditorConfig configuration: indentation is whatever each contributor's editor does."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "unreferenced-dependencies",
      "lines": [
        "7 declared packages are named nowhere in the checkout: eslint-config-standard, eslint-plugin-import, eslint-plugin-node, eslint-plugin-promise, eslint-plugin-standard, file-loader, style-loader.",
        "  Searched as literal names over 761 files, package.json excluded apart from its non-dependency fields, lockfiles excluded; then as an ESLint shorthand, as what TypeScript takes from a tsconfig, and as a peer of an installed package in package-lock.json. A package loaded some other way is not named anywhere either, so this is a list to check, not a list to remove."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "license-drift",
      "lines": [
        "Licence AGPL (appinfo/info.xml), AGPL-3.0-or-later (composer.json).",
        "  AGPL in appinfo/info.xml is a deprecated App Store value, shown there as AGPLv3+, which is AGPL-3.0-or-later. An SPDX id there needs a <nextcloud> min-version of 31 or higher.",
        "  No LICENSES/ directory, so the licence text itself is not in the checkout, which is what REUSE and the distributions check for."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
